WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_kfk_111'), 'The team plans to double the partitions of the topic while orders keep flowing:

```text
$ kafka-topics --bootstrap-server kafka:9092 --alter --topic orders.v1 --partitions 24
$ kafka-topics --bootstrap-server kafka:9092 --describe --topic orders.v1 | head -1
Topic: orders.v1  PartitionCount: 24  ReplicationFactor: 3  Configs: min.insync.replicas=2
```

Statement: "After the change many order ids map to a different partition, so an order placed before the change can have its later events in a new partition and, for a while, be read out of order."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The default partitioner computes the key''s murmur2 hash modulo the partition count, so most keys move when the count goes from 12 to 24. Events already written stay where they are; the next events of the same order go to the new partition, and a consumer of that partition can process them before the old partition''s consumer has caught up. Kafka can add partitions but never removes them. Pick the count up front, with room to grow, or switch over during a quiet window.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_kfk_111') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
