Statement: "With acks=all the producer does not count a write as done while fewer than 2 replicas are in sync; the error is retriable, so the api''s event is written once a follower is back in sync, while the acks=1 writes are held by one broker only."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. min.insync.replicas is the number of in-sync replicas a write with acks=all needs. With only the leader in the ISR, the broker rejects such writes with NotEnoughReplicas, a retriable error, and the producer keeps retrying within delivery.timeout.ms. Producers with acks=1 are not affected by the setting, so the analytics importer keeps writing records that exist on one broker only until the followers catch up. The misconception is that min.insync.replicas protects every producer of the topic.', 3, 5
