Statement: "The three extra pods will start sharing the busiest partitions once the next rebalance finishes, so adding pods beyond 6 still adds read throughput."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Within one consumer group a partition is read by at most one member at a time; that is how Kafka keeps the records of one key in order. orders.v1 has 6 partitions, so a 7th, 8th and 9th member get no partitions and sit idle, whatever the assignor does. To read faster with more pods, add partitions (which moves keys to new partitions, see lesson 1) or make each record cheaper to handle. Capping the HPA at the partition count avoids paying for idle pods.', 1, 5
