```text
11:42:07 relay  published 3 rows (ids 418-420) to orders.v1
11:42:07 relay  SIGKILL (pod evicted)
11:42:21 relay  started, producer enable.idempotence=true
11:42:22 relay  published 3 rows (ids 418-420) to orders.v1
11:42:22 courier-matcher  event o-2002:1 already processed, skipping
```

Statement: "With `enable.idempotence=true` on the producer, the broker drops the second copy of rows 418-420, so the consumer never sees a duplicate."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. An idempotent producer removes duplicates caused by its own retries: the broker tracks the producer id and a sequence number per partition and ignores a resent batch from the same producer session. The restarted relay is a new producer instance with a new producer id, re-reading rows it never marked as sent, so the broker stores them again. The outbox gives at-least-once delivery; the consumer has to dedupe by the event id, as the courier-matcher does in the last log line.', 2, 5
