Statement: "BACKWARD means consumers still on the old schema can read events written with the new one, so this order (producer first, consumers a week later) is exactly what BACKWARD protects."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. BACKWARD guarantees the opposite direction: the NEW schema can read data written with the OLD one, which is what you need when consumers upgrade first. Old consumers reading new events is FORWARD compatibility. Here adding an optional field happens to be safe both ways, but BACKWARD did not check it: a change that passes BACKWARD (for example dropping a field that the old consumers require) can break the old consumers in this plan. Producers-first releases need FORWARD or FULL. The misconception is reading "backward" as "old consumers keep working".', 1, 5
